{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/shortestpaths\/astarsearchevent"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Enumeration","externalID":"s:13ShortestPaths16AStarSearchEventO","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AStarSearchEvent"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ShortestPaths\/AStarSearch.swift#L18","fileName":"AStarSearch.swift"},"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AStarSearchEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"ShortestPaths"}],"title":"AStarSearchEvent","symbolKind":"enum"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/AStarSearchEvent"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths"]]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What an A* search reports, in order, with the events of the Boost Graph Library’s A* visitor."}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Enumeration Cases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/AStarSearchEvent\/discover(_:distance:estimate:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/AStarSearchEvent\/edgeNotRelaxed(_:distance:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/AStarSearchEvent\/edgeRelaxed(_:distance:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/AStarSearchEvent\/examine(_:distance:estimate:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/AStarSearchEvent\/examineEdge(_:distance:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/AStarSearchEvent\/finish(_:distance:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/AStarSearchEvent\/reopen(_:distance:estimate:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Enumeration-Cases"},{"title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/AStarSearchEvent\/CustomStringConvertible-Implementations","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/AStarSearchEvent\/Equatable-Implementations"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/SQ","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/SH","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AStarSearchEvent","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edge","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Weight","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edge","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The source is discovered first, at distance zero, with its estimate: the heuristic’s guess at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its distance to the target (zero for the target itself). Then, while a vertex is open, the one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with the smallest distance plus estimate is examined (closed). When that is the target the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"search ends there. Otherwise each of its out-edges is examined in turn with the distance it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"offers its target, the examined vertex’s distance plus the edge’s weight, and is then relaxed,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when the offer is smaller than the target’s distance or the target was not yet discovered, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not relaxed. A relaxed edge to an undiscovered vertex is followed by that vertex’s discovery;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one to a closed vertex, which only an inconsistent heuristic allows, by its reopening (the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Boost Graph Library’s black target), after which it is examined again. After its last out-edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the examined vertex is finished. When the target is never reached the search ends once no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex is open."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"doc://ShortestPaths/SQ":{"title":"Swift.Equatable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/SQ"},"doc://ShortestPaths/s8SendableP":{"title":"Swift.Sendable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s8SendableP"},"doc://ShortestPaths/s9EscapableP":{"title":"Swift.Escapable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s9EscapableP"},"doc://ShortestPaths/documentation/ShortestPaths/AStarSearchEvent/examineEdge(_:distance:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/AStarSearchEvent\/examineEdge(_:distance:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An out-edge of the vertex being examined is read; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distance"},{"type":"text","text":" is what it offers its target."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/shortestpaths\/astarsearchevent\/exam